  "worked_solution": "First, notice that our expression is a perfect square that can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{4}\u2061({15}^{\u2218})-2{cos}^{2}\u2061({15}^{\u2218}){sin}^{2}\u2061({15}^{\u2218})+{sin}^{4}\u2061({15}^{\u2218}) & ={({cos}^{2}\u2061({15}^{\u2218})-{sin}^{2}\u2061({15}^{\u2218}))}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}\u2061x-{sin}^{2}\u2061x=\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={15}^{\u2218}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}\u2061({15}^{\u2218})-{sin}^{2}\u2061({15}^{\u2218}) & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\cdot {15}^{\u2218}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061({30}^{\u2218}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({cos}^{2}\u2061({15}^{\u2218})-{sin}^{2}\u2061({15}^{\u2218}))}^{2} & ={(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
